module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.AssociatedModuleFreeComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.GlobalPresentationComparison

/-!
# A globally presented module on a site of schemes over `S` is an `Fᵃ`

Let `S` be a scheme and let a site `C` of schemes over `S` satisfy the four conditions of
Tag 03OJ.  The third assertion of that tag is that **every** quasi-coherent `𝒪`-module on the
site is isomorphic to `Fᵃ` for a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `F`; the source's proof reduces it
to the case of a module admitting a *global* presentation, by Tag 03DN, and then glues the local
answers by fpqc descent.

**This file proves that reduced case**, with no descent step: a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on the site
which is the cokernel of a morphism of free sheaves of `𝒪`-modules lies in the essential image of
`Stacks.Sites.associatedSheafFunctor`.  It is the composite of the three pieces that stand
already:

* step one, `Stacks.Sites.isIso_freeAssociatedComparison`, identifies the free sheaf of
  `𝒪`-modules on `L` with `(⊕_L 𝒪_S)ᵃ`;
* the free-source case of Descent, Lemma 0GN7 over an arbitrary base,
  `Stacks.Sites.exists_siteAssociatedModuleMap_free_comp`, writes the presenting morphism between
  free sheaves as `φᵃ` for a morphism `φ : ⊕_{L'} 𝒪_S ⟶ ⊕_L 𝒪_S` of modules on `S`, compatibly
  with those two identifications;
* step two, `Stacks.Sites.isIso_cokernelAssociatedComparison`, identifies the cokernel of `φᵃ`,
  taken in the sheaves of `𝒪`-modules on the site, with `coker(φ)ᵃ`.

So the module is `coker(φ)ᵃ`, and `coker φ` is the quasi-coherent module on `S` the assertion
asks for.  The Zariski-refinement condition (2) of the tag is the only geometric hypothesis used,
and it is used only inside those three inputs.

## The sheaf conditions

Three associated presheaves have to be sheaves for the statement to be formed at all — those of
`⊕_L 𝒪_S`, of `⊕_{L'} 𝒪_S` and of `coker φ` — and the last of them names a module produced
*inside* the proof.  So the hypothesis is carried in the uniform shape
`Stacks.Sites.associatedSheafFunctor` already uses: the associated presheaf of **every**
quasi-coherent module on `S` is a sheaf on the site.  That is exactly the second assertion of
Tag 03OJ, and on a site whose coverings are fpqc coverings of schemes it is a theorem,
`AlgebraicGeometry.isSheaf_associatedPresheaf_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage`; condition (4) of the tag
is therefore not carried here, and enters only through that hypothesis.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_isColimit`: **a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on the
  site exhibited as a cokernel of a morphism of free sheaves of `𝒪`-modules is an `Fᵃ`.**
* `Stacks.Sites.essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_presentation`: the same with the presentation
  given as Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.Presentation`.
* `Stacks.Sites.essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_hasGlobalPresentation`: the same with the
  presentation given as `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`, which is the shape Tag 03DN
  produces.  The passage between the two encodings is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation`, and it is where the
  essential smallness of the site is used a second time.

## Implementation notes

**Why the topology is a parameter and not `K.toGrothendieck`.**  The three statements below are
read at a Grothendieck topology `J` together with an equation `J = K.toGrothendieck`, which is
the same strength as reading them at `K.toGrothendieck` itself — instantiate `J` there and the
equation by `rfl`.  The generality is what the slice step needs and the reason is a type
mismatch and not mathematics: the localization of a topology at an object, `J.over X`, and the
topology generated by the comapped precoverage, `(K.comap (Over.forget X)).toGrothendieck`, are
*equal*
(`CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget`), but `Sheaf J₁ RingCat` and
`Sheaf J₂ RingCat` are different *types* for equal-but-not-definitionally-equal `J₁`, `J₂`, so a
module restricted to a slice — which Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.over` produces over `J.over X` —
cannot be fed to a statement spelled with the generated topology.  With the topology a parameter
it can, and the equation is discharged by `subst` inside each proof, which is why every proof
below opens with it.  See
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.AssociatedModuleSliceEssImage`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is claimed.  The third assertion of Tag 03OJ is the statement for an
arbitrary quasi-coherent module; the globally presented case is a step of its proof, as steps one
and two are, and the registrations of the tag stay the two in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.QuasiCoherent.FpqcCoveringSiteSheaves`.

`EssentiallySmall.{u} C` is carried for the same reason as in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.AssociatedModuleFreeComparison`, whose module
documentation explains at length why it is condition (1) of the tag and not a strengthening of
it: it is what supplies sheafification of abelian presheaves on the site, without which
`SheafOfModules.free` — a coproduct taken in sheaves — does not exist.  The three sheafification
classes it supplies are declared `local instance` here because they are `local instance` there;
all three are propositions, so nothing depends on which proof of them is in scope.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03OJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03OJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GN7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GN7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Sites

open _root_.AlgebraicGeometry

variable (S : Scheme.{u}) {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u} C] [EssentiallySmall.{u} C]
  (toOver : C ⥤ Over S) (K : Precoverage C)

/-! ### The sheafification classes

`Stacks.Sites.hasWeakSheafify_toGrothendieck`, `…wEqualsLocallyBijective_toGrothendieck` and
`…hasSheafify_toGrothendieck` are `local instance` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.AssociatedModuleFreeComparison`, so importing that file
does not bring them into scope here.  Restating them would be a second declaration of the same
fact under a primed name, which is what the standing order against duplicates forbids — and
`newdups` does flag it.  Instead the three general theorems that each of them is a one-line
application of are registered as local instances directly.  Their shared hypothesis is the
`[EssentiallySmall.{u} C]` of the variable block above, which is condition (1) of the tag. -/

attribute [local instance] CategoryTheory.hasWeakSheafify_addCommGrpCat_of_essentiallySmall
  CategoryTheory.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat_of_essentiallySmall
  CategoryTheory.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat_of_essentiallySmall

variable [toOver.Full] [toOver.Faithful]
  (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (hJ : J = K.toGrothendieck)
  (hR : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structurePresheaf S toOver))
  (hSh : ∀ (M : S.Modules) (_ : M.IsQuasicoherent),
    Presheaf.IsSheaf J (associatedPresheaf S M toOver))
  (e : C) [IsIso (toOver.obj e).hom]

/-- The cokernel of a morphism of free modules on a scheme is quasi-coherent.  An instance, so
that `Stacks.Sites.siteAssociatedModule` of such a cokernel can be written. -/
public instance isQuasicoherent_cokernel_free {X : Scheme.{u}} {L L' : Type u}
    (φ : SheafOfModules.free (R := X.ringCatSheaf) L' ⟶
      SheafOfModules.free (R := X.ringCatSheaf) L) :
    (cokernel (C := X.Modules) φ).IsQuasicoherent :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentColimits.isQuasicoherent_cokernel (X := X) φ

include e hJ hSh in
/-- **A sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on a site of schemes over `S` which is a cokernel of a morphism of
free sheaves of `𝒪`-modules is `coker(φ)ᵃ` for a morphism `φ` of free modules on `S`.**  This is
the third assertion of Tag 03OJ for a module carrying a global presentation, which is the case the
source's proof reduces the assertion to by Tag 03DN, with the witness exhibited.

The presenting morphism `α : ⊕_{L'} 𝒪 ⟶ ⊕_L 𝒪` of free sheaves on the site is `φᵃ` for a
morphism `φ : ⊕_{L'} 𝒪_S ⟶ ⊕_L 𝒪_S` of free modules on `S`, by the free-source case of
Descent, Lemma 0GN7 over an arbitrary base
(`Stacks.Sites.exists_siteAssociatedModuleMap_free_comp`), compatibly with the two comparison
morphisms of step one, which step one
(`Stacks.Sites.isIso_freeAssociatedComparison`) makes isomorphisms; so the cokernel of `α` is the
cokernel of `φᵃ`.  Step two (`Stacks.Sites.isIso_cokernelAssociatedComparison`) identifies that
cokernel with `coker(φ)ᵃ`.  The Zariski-refinement condition (2) of the tag is the only
hypothesis beyond the sheaf conditions.

The witness is recorded as a cokernel of free modules, and not merely as some quasi-coherent
module, because the gluing step of the tag consumes exactly that shape: Descent, Lemma 0GN7 over
an arbitrary base is available for such a source
(`Stacks.Sites.bijective_associatedModuleMap_cokernel`). -/
public theorem exists_cokernel_iso_of_isColimit
    (hZariski : ∀ (T : C) (R : Presieve ((toOver.obj T).left)),
      R ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage.{u} ((toOver.obj T).left) →
        ∃ Q : Presieve T, Q ∈ K T ∧
          Presieve.map (toOver ⋙ Over.forget S) Q ≤ (Sieve.generate R).arrows)
    (L L' : Type u)
    {𝒢 : SheafOfModules.{u} (siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR)}
    (α : SheafOfModules.free (R := siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR) L' ⟶
      SheafOfModules.free (R := siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR) L)
    (p : SheafOfModules.free (R := siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR) L ⟶ 𝒢)
    (hp : α ≫ p = 0) (hcok : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ p hp)) :
    ∃ φ : SheafOfModules.free (R := S.ringCatSheaf) L' ⟶
        SheafOfModules.free (R := S.ringCatSheaf) L,
      Nonempty (siteAssociatedModule S (cokernel (C := S.Modules) φ) toOver J hR
        (hSh _ inferInstance)
          ≅ 𝒢) := by
  subst hJ
  have hFL := hSh (SheafOfModules.free (R := S.ringCatSheaf) L) inferInstance
  have hFL' := hSh (SheafOfModules.free (R := S.ringCatSheaf) L') inferInstance
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ :=
    exists_siteAssociatedModuleMap_free_comp S toOver K L hR hFL e L' hFL' hZariski α
  have hH := hSh (cokernel (C := S.Modules) φ) inferInstance
  have h₁ := isIso_freeAssociatedComparison S toOver K L hR hFL e hZariski
  have h₂ := isIso_freeAssociatedComparison S toOver K L' hR hFL' e hZariski
  have h₃ := isIso_cokernelAssociatedComparison S toOver K hR φ hFL' hFL hH hZariski
  refine ⟨φ, ⟨?_⟩⟩
  refine (hcok.coconePointUniqueUpToIso (colimit.isColimit (parallelPair α 0)) ≪≫ ?_).symm
  refine cokernel.mapIso α (siteAssociatedModuleMap S toOver K hR φ hFL' hFL)
    (@asIso _ _ _ _ (freeAssociatedComparison S toOver K L' hR hFL' e) h₂)
    (@asIso _ _ _ _ (freeAssociatedComparison S toOver K L hR hFL e) h₁) hφ.symm ≪≫ ?_
  exact @asIso _ _ _ _ (cokernelAssociatedComparison S toOver K hR φ hFL' hFL hH) h₃

include e hJ in
/-- **A sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on a site of schemes over `S` which is a cokernel of a morphism of
free sheaves of `𝒪`-modules is an `Fᵃ`.**  This is
`Stacks.Sites.exists_cokernel_iso_of_isColimit` with the witness forgotten. -/
public theorem essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_isColimit
    (hZariski : ∀ (T : C) (R : Presieve ((toOver.obj T).left)),
      R ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage.{u} ((toOver.obj T).left) →
        ∃ Q : Presieve T, Q ∈ K T ∧
          Presieve.map (toOver ⋙ Over.forget S) Q ≤ (Sieve.generate R).arrows)
    (L L' : Type u)
    {𝒢 : SheafOfModules.{u} (siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR)}
    (α : SheafOfModules.free (R := siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR) L' ⟶
      SheafOfModules.free (R := siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR) L)
    (p : SheafOfModules.free (R := siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR) L ⟶ 𝒢)
    (hp : α ≫ p = 0) (hcok : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ p hp)) :
    (associatedSheafFunctor S toOver J hR hSh).essImage 𝒢 := by
  obtain ⟨φ, ⟨i⟩⟩ := exists_cokernel_iso_of_isColimit S toOver K J hJ hR hSh e hZariski L L' α p
    hp hcok
  exact ⟨⟨cokernel (C := S.Modules) φ, inferInstance⟩, ⟨i⟩⟩

include e hJ hSh in
/-- **A sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on a site of schemes over `S` admitting a
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` is `coker(φ)ᵃ` for a morphism `φ` of free modules on
`S`.**  The two encodings of a global presentation agree on an essentially small site, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation`, and the presentation's
relations morphism and cokernel diagram feed `Stacks.Sites.exists_cokernel_iso_of_isColimit`. -/
public theorem exists_cokernel_iso_of_hasGlobalPresentation
    (hZariski : ∀ (T : C) (R : Presieve ((toOver.obj T).left)),
      R ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage.{u} ((toOver.obj T).left) →
        ∃ Q : Presieve T, Q ∈ K T ∧
          Presieve.map (toOver ⋙ Over.forget S) Q ≤ (Sieve.generate R).arrows)
    {𝒢 : SheafOfModules.{u} (siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR)}
    (h : 𝒢.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    ∃ (L L' : Type u) (φ : SheafOfModules.free (R := S.ringCatSheaf) L' ⟶
        SheafOfModules.free (R := S.ringCatSheaf) L),
      Nonempty (siteAssociatedModule S (cokernel (C := S.Modules) φ) toOver J hR
        (hSh _ inferInstance)
          ≅ 𝒢) := by
  subst hJ
  have P := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation h).some
  exact ⟨_, _, exists_cokernel_iso_of_isColimit S toOver K K.toGrothendieck rfl hR hSh e
    hZariski P.generators.I P.relations.I (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom P)
    P.generators.π (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π P)
    P.isColimit⟩

include e hJ in
/-- **A sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on a site of schemes over `S` admitting a
`SheafOfModules.Presentation` is an `Fᵃ`.**  The presenting morphism between free sheaves of
`𝒪`-modules is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom` and the cokernel diagram is
`SheafOfModules.Presentation.isColimit`, so this is
`Stacks.Sites.essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_isColimit` read at those two. -/
public theorem essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_presentation
    (hZariski : ∀ (T : C) (R : Presieve ((toOver.obj T).left)),
      R ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage.{u} ((toOver.obj T).left) →
        ∃ Q : Presieve T, Q ∈ K T ∧
          Presieve.map (toOver ⋙ Over.forget S) Q ≤ (Sieve.generate R).arrows)
    {𝒢 : SheafOfModules.{u} (siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR)}
    (P : 𝒢.Presentation) :
    (associatedSheafFunctor S toOver J hR hSh).essImage 𝒢 := by
  subst hJ
  exact essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_isColimit S toOver K K.toGrothendieck rfl hR hSh e
    hZariski P.generators.I P.relations.I (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom P)
    P.generators.π (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π P)
    P.isColimit

include e hJ in
/-- **A sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on a site of schemes over `S` admitting a
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` is an `Fᵃ`.**  This is the shape Tag 03DN produces on the
members of a covering family of the final object, and so the form in which the third assertion of
Tag 03OJ consumes the globally presented case.

The two encodings of a global presentation agree on an essentially small site, by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation`. -/
public theorem essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_hasGlobalPresentation
    (hZariski : ∀ (T : C) (R : Presieve ((toOver.obj T).left)),
      R ∈ Scheme.zariskiPrecoverage.{u} ((toOver.obj T).left) →
        ∃ Q : Presieve T, Q ∈ K T ∧
          Presieve.map (toOver ⋙ Over.forget S) Q ≤ (Sieve.generate R).arrows)
    {𝒢 : SheafOfModules.{u} (siteStructureSheaf S toOver J hR)}
    (h : 𝒢.HasGlobalPresentation) :
    (associatedSheafFunctor S toOver J hR hSh).essImage 𝒢 := by
  subst hJ
  exact essImage_associatedSheafFunctor_of_presentation S toOver K K.toGrothendieck rfl hR hSh e
    hZariski (Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation h).some


end Stacks.Sites

end
